        "\n",
        "### 6. 🧠 Model Selection, Training, & Comparison (Step 5 & 5.1)\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase involved training and evaluating various machine learning models to identify the best performer for the ordinal classification task, with a strong focus on the Quadratic Weighted Kappa (QWK) metric. Initially, the notebook text indicated `LinearSVC` as the primary model based on prior research, but the comprehensive tuning loop then determined the actually *best performing* model for this specific dataset and split.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Models Explored & Tuned (using `RandomizedSearchCV` with 5-fold `StratifiedKFold` and QWK scoring):**\n",
        "\n",
        "*   **Logistic Regression**: A linear baseline model for classification.\n",
        "*   **Decision Tree**: A non-linear, interpretable model.\n",
        "*   **Random Forest**: An ensemble of decision trees, known for robustness.\n",
        "*   **Gradient Boosting**: An ensemble that builds trees sequentially, correcting errors of previous trees.\n",
        "*   **LinearSVC**: Support Vector Classifier with a linear kernel, chosen for its strong performance in past research on similar datasets.\n",
        "*   **AdaBoost**: An ensemble boosting algorithm.\n",
        "*   **Gaussian Naive Bayes**: A probabilistic classifier.\n",
        "*   **XGBoost**: A highly optimized gradient boosting implementation.\n",
        "*   **LightGBM**: Another efficient gradient boosting framework.\n",
        "*   **OrdinalRoundingClassifier (Custom `OrdinalGB`)**: A custom-built ordinal-aware regressor that uses `GradientBoostingRegressor` internally and rounds predictions to the nearest valid ordinal class (0-3). This model was treated as a baseline and evaluated directly due to its custom nature.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Hyperparameters & Tuning**: For each model, a search space for key hyperparameters (e.g., `n_estimators`, `max_depth`, `learning_rate`, `C`) was defined. `RandomizedSearchCV` was used to efficiently explore these spaces, optimizing for the `qwk_scorer`.\n",
        "\n",
