        "\n",
        "**Theoretical Details of the Top Models:**\n",
        "\n",
        "*   **OrdinalRoundingClassifier (OrdinalGB)**:\n",
        "    *   **How it works**: This is a custom approach designed specifically for ordinal classification. It wraps a standard `GradientBoostingRegressor` (`sklearn.ensemble.GradientBoostingRegressor`). Instead of directly classifying, the regressor predicts a continuous numerical score. These continuous scores are then **rounded** to the nearest integer, which corresponds to the ordinal classes (0, 1, 2, 3). This method implicitly respects the ordinal nature of the target variable by treating the classes as ordered numerical values during the prediction phase.\n",
        "    *   **Hyperparameters (for the internal `GradientBoostingRegressor`)**:\n",
        "        *   `n_estimators`: The number of boosting stages (individual decision trees) to perform. Higher values can lead to better performance but also to overfitting. (e.g., 300 in the custom class).\n",
        "        *   `max_depth`: The maximum depth of the individual regression estimators. Controls the complexity of the trees. Deeper trees can capture more complex patterns but are prone to overfitting. (e.g., 4 in the custom class).\n",
        "        *   `learning_rate`: Shrinks the contribution of each tree by `learning_rate`. There is a trade-off between `learning_rate` and `n_estimators`. (e.g., 0.05 in the custom class).\n",
        "        *   `subsample`: The fraction of samples to be used for fitting the individual base learners. Can reduce variance. (e.g., 0.8).\n",
        "\n",
